# Monotone ratchet ceiling for `cargo xtask lint-unbounded-wait`
# (bd rc-3lx2, ADR-0069 §13.2 R1; mirror of ratchet-test-sleep.max, bd
# rc-c9r6w, and ratchet-cancel-tokens.max, bd rc-pu2s).
#
# The integer below is the maximum allowed count of unadjudicated
# unbounded waits in test function bodies across crates/, scripts/,
# examples/, benchmarks/, fuzz/. Detector classes (V1): awaited
# recv/lock/acquire/wait/join_next/connect method calls, blocking_recv,
# tokio::spawn/spawn_blocking/JoinSet::spawn awaits (incl. awaited
# spawned-handle bindings), tokio::net::TcpStream::connect awaits, and
# await-carrying `loop`s with no deadline. A wait inside the future
# argument of tokio::time::timeout/timeout_at is bounded (imports and
# aliases resolved); a loop with a per-iteration timeout call is bounded.
# Sites marked `// allow-test-wait: <reason>` (ADR-0069 R1 normative
# marker) are suppressed at scan time and never count toward the ceiling.
# Known blind spots (documented in the module doc): stream I/O
# (read/write/flush awaits), sync blocking waits, method-form deadlines
# (fut.timeout(d)), and awaits embedded in macro bodies (tokio::select!
# / join! arms — opaque token streams to syn). The number may only
# DECREASE — never raise it without review justification; the diff on
# this file is the regression signal.
#
# Seed reconciliation (2026-09-21, bd rc-3lx2): the pre-adjudication
# lexical `loop{`-without-`timeout` scan reports 157 sites; the
# structural scan reports 548. Diff: 517 new true positives (waits the
# lexical scan cannot see: recv/lock/spawn-handle/connect awaits), 31
# lexical+structural loop overlaps, 126 lexical-only sites — sampled 8,
# all false positives (`loop` matched in comments, string literals,
# YAML/JSON fixtures, and embedded script source). Stream I/O
# (read/write/flush awaits) is deferred to a later detector revision;
# adding it is a deliberate, review-visible ceiling bump.
#
# Loopsweep burn-down (2026-09-21, bd rc-w32w7): 32 converted (23 enclosing-timeout R-P1 + 9 retry-wrap R-P3), 5 allow-test-wait markers (spawned accept-loop servers); 548 -> 511.
